# Unit-sizing heuristic configuration (provisional, uncalibrated — see issue #325)
#
# Adjusts the per-unit ceiling for parallelizing plan steps, counting distinct files,
# and action-plan findings into work units.
#
# Config cascade: built-in defaults < ~/.claude/unit-sizing-heuristic.yaml
# < <project-root>/.claude/unit-sizing-heuristic.yaml
#
# All values must be positive integers. Non-numeric or zero values are silently
# ignored and fall back to the built-in default, with a warning on stderr.
#
# Built-in defaults (provisional):
#   steps_per_unit: 8
#   files_per_unit: 12
#   findings_per_unit: 16
#
# Example (adjust ceilings for your project):
# steps_per_unit: 10
# files_per_unit: 15
# findings_per_unit: 20
